# MY AI BRAIN — environment variables. Copy to .env.local for local development.
# Real values go in .env.local (gitignored) and in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# None of these reach the browser. The page talks only to its own /api functions, and those talk to
# Supabase with the signed-in user's session, so row level security applies to every query.

# ── SERVER-ONLY (read by the /api functions) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase → Project Settings → API → Project URL
SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys → the anon key (or the newer "publishable" key, sb_publishable_…).
# Safe to be public by design, but this app keeps it server-side anyway.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# The site's own URL, used for OAuth and magic-link redirects. Leave empty locally (the request's host
# is used); set it in production, e.g. https://my-ai-brain.vercel.app or your custom domain.
SITE_URL=

# ── NOT USED — never add these here or to Vercel ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   bypasses RLS; nothing in this app needs it
# Google / GitHub OAuth client secrets live in Supabase → Authentication → Providers, not in this app
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* / any public variable: the browser needs no configuration at all

# ── OPTIONAL (only for `npm run import -- --llm`, the local Claude pass; never deployed) ──────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
